const concepts=[['Invoice','A commercial and accounting document that establishes the customer’s payment obligation.','€10,000 for products delivered.'],['Receivable','A recognised financial claim on a customer, carried as an asset until settled or adjusted.','The unpaid €10,000.'],['Due date','The contractual maturity date derived from the invoice date and agreed payment terms.','30 days after the invoice.'],['Overdue','A receivable that remains open beyond its contractual maturity date.','Payment is still missing on day 31.'],['Credit note','A controlled accounting adjustment that reduces an invoiced balance.','€20,000 for returned goods.'],['Dispute','A customer-raised challenge that requires validation and resolution before settlement.','100 cases billed; only 90 received.'],['Deduction','A short payment taken by the customer against the invoiced amount, whether authorised or contested.','A promotion amount is subtracted.'],['Promise to pay','A dated customer commitment that supports follow-up, forecasting and reliability assessment.','“We will pay on Friday.”'],['Collection case','The governed work object linking exposure, evidence, activity, ownership and outcome.','Invoices, context, actions and outcome together.'],['Business partner','The external legal or commercial entity represented by a governed master-data identity in SAP.','Customer C123 buys products from NorthStar and owes payment.'],['Company code','The legal-accounting entity in which receivables and related financial documents are posted.','Invoice 4711 for C123 is posted to company code 1000.'],['Collection segment','The organisational scope used to structure collection responsibility and access across company codes.','SEG-UK-1 maps to company codes 1000 and 2000; partner assignment determines which customers Alan handles.']];
